OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AAt least 68 killed in Spanish
OL,4,Ahigh-speed train crash, as prime
OL,5,Aminister says 'whole country is
OL,6,Agrieving'
OL,7,
OL,8,FThe rail operator Iryo says its train
OL,9,Fwas "struck from behind" by a Renfe
OL,10,Ftrain. More than 500 passengers were
OL,11,Ftravelling on the two trains
OL,13,FSpeaking at the crash site, Prime
OL,14,FMinister Pedro Sanchez says Spain is
OL,15,F"grieving" - most major parties have
OL,16,Fsuspended general election campaigning
OL,18,FWitnesses have described "terrible"
OL,19,Fscenes, while Roberto Gomez, a Spanish
OL,20,Fjournalist travelling on one of the
OL,21,Ftrains, says it was "extremely chaotic
OL,22,Fand very distressing"
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
